    [BugFix][KVPool] Remove stale Memcache init barrier arguments (#20321)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    `KVPoolWorker.__init__` no longer accepts `memcache_dp_init_barrier`,
    but the AscendStore factory still forwards it as a keyword and
    `LayerwiseKVPoolWorker` still forwards it positionally. Bulk
    construction therefore raises an unexpected-keyword `TypeError`, and
    direct layerwise construction passes too many positional arguments.
    
    Remove the stale parameters and forwarding from both callers. This does
    not reintroduce or change the removed barrier implementation and
    contains no QSA cache-layout, MTP or transfer changes.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. AscendStore bulk/layerwise worker construction no longer fails
    because of the removed argument. Included
    `release_notes/fragments/20321.yaml`.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - With the new constructor regressions applied to unmodified main
    `0be0a615`, both test methods fail: factory argument forwarding and
    signature-checked layerwise superclass delegation.
    - After the cleanup, **170 passed**, exit 0, with CI-pinned vLLM
    `544f182d`:
      ```bash
      python -m pytest -q \
        tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_pool_worker.py \
        tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_ascend_store_connector.py
      ```
    - Python syntax and `git diff --check` passed. The factory test covers
    bulk and layerwise selection; superclass delegation is checked using the
    real base constructor signature.
    - CPU unit validation only; no NPU model test or performance claim. CI
    and independent review remain pending.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
